course: dictionary
lesson: 11904
title: Meet the bullfrog
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A bullfrog is a very large frog. The word is made of two parts: bull, which suggests something big and strong, and frog. «The bullfrog sat on a lily pad by the pond.» Lily pads and ponds tell you it is an animal that lives near water.
explain: Some words describe a sound. A bullfrog has a deep, loud call that sounds like a bull or a cow mooing. «We heard a deep moo from the pond, and it was a bullfrog.» The clue is the sound: deep and loud, not high and tinkling.
explain: Context also tells you about life and food. «A bullfrog starts life as a tiny tadpole and grows bigger each week.» Tadpoles are young frogs, so the sentence shows that the bullfrog grows up from a tadpole. Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and asking if it still makes sense.
fact: A bullfrog is a very large frog.
fact: «Bullfrog» is a noun, and its plural is bullfrogs.
fact: A bullfrog's deep, loud call sounds like a bull or a cow mooing.
fact: Bullfrogs grow from big tadpoles, and they eat insects, fish and even small birds.
fact: In some countries the bullfrog is an invasive species, which means it harms local frogs.
exercise: «The bullfrog sat on a lily pad by the pond.» What is a bullfrog? | A fish with a loud call | *A very large frog | A small flower | A bull that lives in a pond
exercise: «A bullfrog starts life as a tiny tadpole.» Where does a bullfrog start its life? | As a fully grown frog | As a fish | As a bird | *As a tadpole
exercise: Sam heard a deep, loud call from the pond. It sounded like a bull or a cow mooing. What was it? | *A bullfrog | A car horn | A bird singing sweetly | A bell ringing
test: «The bullfrog ate insects, fish and even small birds.» What did the bullfrog eat? | *Insects, fish and small birds | Only grass and leaves | Stones from the bottom of the pond | Only seeds from the flowers
test: In some countries the bullfrog is an invasive species. What does this suggest? | It is a tiny frog that never grows | It is a friendly animal that lives only on farms | It only lives in the sea | *It is not from there, and it harms local frogs
exam: Which word means a very large frog with a deep, loud call? | Pond | Toad | Tadpole | *Bullfrog
